is free after 40 years in an Israeli  prison friends and family gathered in  ARA to welcome him home Eunice was the  longest held Palestinian prisoner he and  his cousin Kareem were arrested in 1983  and convicted of murdering an Israeli  soldier Kareem was released two weeks  ago  the first thing Eunice did was a visit  to his father's grave he died 12 years  ago  I always hoped when I was free to see my  homeland liberated Eunice was born in  ahara in 1958 just 10 years after the  nakeda when hundreds of thousands of  Palestinians either fled over forced  from the homes to make way for Jewish  settlers when Israel was founded in 1948  his parents chose to stay and later  became Palestinian citizens of Israel  with that Eunice says she can't believe  she lived to see her son a free man how  do you feel like I just needed his hug  this is the best feeling ever  the celebrations were quite Palestinians  are not allowed to have loud parties or  even fly the national flag by order of  the new Israeli security minister  etymar bengiver  Eunice is viewed here as a symbol of  Palestinian resistance to the Israeli  occupation  he was telling reporters and family  members and friends and peace activists  here that despite the fact that he was  freed he felt sorrow for thousands of  Palestinian prisoners who are still an  Israeli prisons  Israel
 

